#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113614 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56467ebe-c7a2-586e-bb58-a5a7db3a157b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113615 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨3,-6 - \\sqrt{2},-11⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113615 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186113615 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5d7050e8-5e7e-5d1d-a4ab-29bc3f6573b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114966 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2394" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114966 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate  $\\lim\\limits_{t \\to 0} \\mathbf{f}(t),$ given that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf f (t) = \\dfrac{1- e^{t}}{\\sin t} \\ \\mathbf {i}+ \\dfrac{\\sin t}{t+t^2} \\ \\mathbf {j} + \\dfrac{ e^{t} - e^{-t}}{\\sin t} \\ \\mathbf {k}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114966 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4e4541ff-5c48-5300-ac29-e48111fee506" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114966 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the limit of our vector function, we compute the limit of each component individually:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{t \\to 0}\\mathbf f(t) = \\left(\\lim_{t \\to 0} \\dfrac{1-e^t}{\\sin t}\\right)\\,\\mathbf i + \\left( \\lim_{t \\to 0} \\dfrac{\\sin t}{t+t^2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf j + \\left( \\lim_{t \\to 0} \\dfrac{e^t-e^{-t}}{\\sin t} \\right)\\,\\mathbf k\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- The first component can be found using L'Hopital's Rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{1-{e}^{t}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{(1-{e}^{t})}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{-{e}^{t}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{e}^{0}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second component can be found using a special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{t+{t}^{2}} & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{t(t+1)} \\\\  & =({lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{1}{t+1})\\cdot ({lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{t}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{0+1})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third component can be found using L'Hopital's Rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{t}-{e}^{-t}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{({e}^{t}-{e}^{-t})}^{′}}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{t}+{e}^{-t}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{0}+{e}^{-0}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+1}{1} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{t \\to 0}\\mathbf f(t) = -\\mathbf i + \\mathbf j +2\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114967 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2395" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114967 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\lim\\limits_{t \\to \\infty} \\| \\mathbf f(t) \\|$ if $\\mathbf f(t)  = \\left\\langle t^{-1}, \\: \\left(1+\\dfrac{3}{t}\\right)^t, \\: \\dfrac{t^2}{1-t^2} \\right\\rangle.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114967 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b5f3f5c9-3d28-5fee-8d67-d49d743ae474" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114967 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the limit of our vector function, we compute the limit of each component individually:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }f(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{t}^{-1},\\,{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{3}{t})}^{t},\\,{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1-{t}^{2}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{t}^{-1} & ={lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{t}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second component can be found using a special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{3}{t})}^{t} & ={lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{[{(1+\\frac{1}{t/3})}^{t/3}]}^{3} \\\\  & ={[{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{t/3})}^{t/3}]}^{3} \\\\  & =[\\,e\\,]^{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1-{t}^{2}} & ={lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-1}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{t \\to \\infty}\\mathbf f(t) = \\left\\langle 0, \\: e^3, \\: -1\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFinally, the limit of $\\left\\| \\mathbf f(t) \\right\\|$ as $t$ approaches $\\infty$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }‖f(t)‖ & =‖{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }f(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖⟨0,\\,{e}^{3},\\,-1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+({e}^{3})^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{6}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114968 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2396" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114968 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $\\displaystyle \\lim_{t \\to 0} \\big[ \\mathbf f(t) - 2 \\mathbf g(t) \\big]$ given that $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t} \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix},\\,g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186114968 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c2055711-815d-5385-8f31-19cc81f20698" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114968 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}{e}^{t} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}t\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\ {e}^{0} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{lim}_{t\\to 0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}1 \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}2t\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}[f(t)-2g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)-2{lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186114969 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2397" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114969 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $\\displaystyle \\lim_{t \\to 2} \\left[\\mathbf f(t) \\cdot \\mathbf g(t)\\right]$ given that $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(2-t)\\,i+\\frac{6}{t}\\,j-4\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114969 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53cccd72-1595-5316-8162-731103c2da28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186114969 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t) & =({lim}_{t\\to 2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\,i+({lim}_{t\\to 2}t)\\,j+({lim}_{t\\to 2}{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)\\,i+2\\,j+{2}^{2}\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,i+2\\,j+4\\,k, \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 2}g(t) & =({lim}_{t\\to 2}(2-t))\\,i+({lim}_{t\\to 2}\\frac{6}{t})\\,j+({lim}_{t\\to 2}(-4))\\,k \\\\  & =(2-2)\\,i+\\frac{6}{2}\\,j+(-4)\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,i+3\\,j-4\\,k \\\\  & =3\\,j-4\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}[f(t)\\cdot g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t)\\cdot {lim}_{t\\to 2}g(t) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,i+2\\,j+4\\,k)\\cdot (3\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 3+4\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115386 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115386 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115386 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115386 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115386 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115386 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115386 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186115765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186115386 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 175921863672